    "text": "Four electric charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi></math> are placed at the corners of a square of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></math> ( see figure ). The electric potential at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, midway between the two charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></math>, is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0056_0e08d1b40be3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 195px;\" />"
